<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <InvariantGlobalization>true</InvariantGlobalization>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- BIO-MOB-005 owns api/features/bio-mob-005/** only. No ProjectReference to
         Biolog.Api.csproj (one-way dependency, scripts/check-module-project-references.sh) and,
         deliberately, no ProjectReference to api/Biolog.Api/Features/DeviceRegistry - device
         resolution is proven through this project's own narrow gateway
         (Domain/IDeviceTenantResolutionGateway.cs), the same discipline every sibling
         device-facing feature's gateway already uses.

         Duplicate detection (AC03) and the human resolution queue (AC04) are deliberately
         self-contained within this project, scanning only this feature's own EnrolmentPackage
         records - not a ProjectReference to bio-idn-005 (BIO-IDN-005's DuplicateReviewService is
         internal to that project and not a declared dependency of this story) or bio-bio-006
         (same reasoning). This mirrors BIO-BIO-006's own precedent exactly: when the closest
         existing dedup/review construct is internal and undeclared, build an independent,
         project-local one rather than reach into a sibling story's owned files.

         This project's own module adapter lives in api/Biolog.Api/Modules/BioMob005Module.cs
         from the start (never written here first), matching every prior story.

         Device authentication (Api/DeviceAuthenticator.cs, Domain credential store) and human
         actor resolution (Api/ActorResolver.cs, Api/ActorProvenanceGate.cs) are both fresh,
         project-local copies of the same shape BIO-MOB-003/BIO-ACC-003 each already establish -
         "each feature project owns its own small primitives rather than a cross-feature
         reference" is this repository's own established convention. -->
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <FrameworkReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.App" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Biolog.Api" />
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Biolog.Features.OfflineEnrolment.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
